From edb566d3365dd76e889c34a5bed4fa2a9b2ea1f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 20:35:36 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(2d): check each contour tab against every cut of its
 level

The tab bridge check compared only the two cuts beside a tab. A later
run of the same ring (a U-turn in a notch) or another ring could pass
nearer than the tool diameter and cut the tab off its stock, with no
note. The shape-mask measurement reads a neck of 0 mm in both cases.

- tab_clear: each tab's line on the ring against all other cuts of the
  tabbed levels. Nearer than D: the loop is held (its tabbed levels cut
  nothing) with a `tabs:` note. Between D and W + D: a `tabs:` note names
  the narrow strip beside the tab.
- tab_bridge: a `tabs:` note when a grown tab covers a picked start.
- tests: the tab neck meter (shape-mask grid), the U-turn and
  second-ring cases, three tabbed levels, the bridge on the true arcs.

Fixes #2561

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
